WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.850
Thunder on a heath.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:06.380
Three hooded figures wait for two
soldiers coming back from battle.

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:07.700
Three greetings.

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.560
The last: "All hail, Macbeth!

5
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.090
that shalt be king hereafter!"

6
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.290
His friend Banquo hears it too, and warns:

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.530
"The instruments of
darkness tell us truths."

8
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:25.020
In Act 4, a vision tells Macbeth that
"none of woman born" shall harm him.

9
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.490
But they never once say the word kill.

10
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.820
So are the witches to blame?

11
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:34.280
In this mission, you'll find out why one
trick with words was big news after the

12
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.930
Gunpowder Plot of 1605.

13
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.490
And you'll see why a Jacobean
audience took witches seriously,

14
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.050
though not everyone believed.

15
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.440
Your mission: decide how
far they are to blame.
